-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ב/5: תשלום תוספת מעונות לעובדי הוראה
-- The daycare addition (תוספת מעונות) from 1.9.2011 for teaching staff of the
-- owners of secondary education, under the framework agreement of 12.1.2011
-- as the general agreement of 14.8.2011 applies it: who is entitled, the
-- amounts for up to two children under 5, pro-rating, the periods it is paid
-- for, its character, and what other arrangements it replaces.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשע"ב/5 תשלום תוספת מעונות לעובדי הוראה`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date (22.9.2011), reference number, addressee, and the lead-in: the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, the general agreement of 14.8.2011 that applies its terms including the daycare addition, a remark that for state-employed teachers an agreement in principle is to be anchored in a collective agreement, and the circular's purpose; no rule of its own.

-- Time is counted in school months of 2011/12 (common.l4: September 2011 = 1).

@desc A teaching employee of an owner, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `daycare employee` HAS
    `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner of secondary education` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a mother`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a widower or divorced man with the children in his custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled through section 4(א) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the right extended to the employee by section 4(א) of that law, which section 2(ז) applies; an input
    `children under 5`                   IS A NUMBER @desc the employee's children who have not reached 5 (in custody, for a father)
    `position fraction`                  IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held (1 = one full position)
    `entitled to salary from the employer and funded by it this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc false in a month of maternity pay from National Insurance or of unpaid leave

DECLARE `daycare action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the daycare addition` HAS `daycare paid` IS A NUMBER
    `require receipts`

§§ `1 תחולה`

-- Section 1(א): women in the teaching-staff grade employed by the owners
-- of secondary education who are mothers of a child or children under 5.
-- Section 1(ב): a widower or divorced man with the child or children in his
-- custody is treated as such an employee.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within section 1` d IF
        d's `in the teaching-staff grade`
    AND d's `employed by an owner of secondary education`
    AND d's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1
    AND (   d's `a mother`
         OR d's `a widower or divorced man with the children in his custody`)

§§ `2 תשלום תוספת מעונות`

-- Section 2(א)(1)–(3): from 1.9.2011, a partial reimbursement of keeping a
-- child in daycare or other supervision, paid to the mother without
-- receipts: 300 ₪ a month for one or the first child, 200 ₪ for the second.
-- Section 2(ג): for two children at most at once.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_c
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full-position daycare amount for` n IS
    BRANCH IF n AT LEAST 2 THEN 500
           IF n AT LEAST 1 THEN 300
           OTHERWISE 0

`the amount for the first child` MEANS 300
`the amount for the second child` MEANS 200
#ASSERT `the full-position daycare amount for` 2 EQUALS `the amount for the first child` PLUS `the amount for the second child`
#ASSERT `the full-position daycare amount for` 4 EQUALS `the full-position daycare amount for` 2

-- Section 2(א)(2): paid to the mother of a child as in section 1, who is
-- not required to produce receipts. The text sets no time limit.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `daycare action`
DECIDE `no receipts` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `require receipts`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 2(א)(2): the mother is not required to produce receipts"

-- Section 2(ב): the amounts are for a full position, pro-rated for a part
-- position. F-2011-12_tashab_05-a: the text does not say what applies above
-- a full position. The reading adopted: a full position's amount at most.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daycare position share` d IS
    min (d's `position fraction`) 1

GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share if pro-rated above a full position too` d IS
    d's `position fraction`

`section 2(ב) leaves a position above full undecided` MEANS
    NOT (`the daycare position share` `a teacher at 120% with one child`
         EQUALS `the share if pro-rated above a full position too` `a teacher at 120% with one child`)
#ASSERT `section 2(ב) leaves a position above full undecided`

-- Section 2(ד): updated each January under the agreements; the new amounts
-- are to be published. This circular's amounts are the ones from 1.9.2011.
@ref akn:art_2__para_d
`the month the amounts are updated` MEANS `month number` January

-- Section 2(ה): only for a period of salary from the employer and funded by
-- it; not for a period of maternity pay or unpaid leave.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e/p1
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a month the addition is paid for` d IF
    d's `entitled to salary from the employer and funded by it this month`

-- Section 2(ו), printed in the corpus as a paragraph of 2(ה): an expense
-- reimbursement, so not salary for every purpose; contributions are made on
-- it as the employer does on an expense-reimbursement component.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e/p2
`the character of the daycare addition` MEANS `daycare character` FALSE TRUE

DECLARE `daycare character` HAS
    `salary for every purpose`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `contributions as on expense reimbursements` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 2(ז): a "right related to parenthood" under section 4(ב) of the
-- Equal Employment Opportunities Law, to which section 4(א) of that law
-- applies; who section 4(א) extends the right to is that law's, an input.
@ref akn:art_2__para_g
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent the addition is paid to` d IF
        `within section 1` d
    OR (    d's `in the teaching-staff grade`
        AND d's `employed by an owner of secondary education`
        AND d's `children under 5` AT LEAST 1
        AND d's `entitled through section 4(א) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law`)

§§ `3 החלפה/ביטול הסדר מעונות אחר`

-- Section 3: from the September 2011 salary the addition replaces every
-- other arrangement for a child under 5, unless a GENERAL arrangement (of the
-- grade, employer, workplace or region) pays another benefit for daycare of
-- more than 300 ₪ for one child AND more than 500 ₪ for two or more; then
-- that arrangement continues on its own rules, judged at the general level.
-- For an employer under section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law, subject to
-- section 29 (an input).
@desc A general arrangement (of the grade, employer, workplace or region) for daycare, judged at the general level, never per employee.
DECLARE `general arrangement` HAS
    `pays another daycare benefit`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `its benefit for one child`          IS A NUMBER @desc shekels a month for one or the first child
    `its benefit for two or more children` IS A NUMBER @desc shekels a month for two or more children
    `section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc true where the employer is not subject to section 29, or section 29 permits the arrangement

@ref akn:art_3__para_b akn:art_3__para_c akn:art_3__para_d akn:art_3__para_f
GIVEN g IS A `general arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general arrangement continues` g IF
        g's `pays another daycare benefit`
    AND g's `its benefit for one child` GREATER THAN 300
    AND g's `its benefit for two or more children` GREATER THAN 500
    AND g's `section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law permits it`

-- F-2011-12_tashab_05-b: section 3(ה) keeps the general arrangement but
-- does not say whether the daycare addition is then paid besides it. The
-- reading adopted: it is not — the addition is paid where it replaces the
-- other arrangements (section 3(א)), and the better arrangement is kept
-- instead of it.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a akn:art_3__para_e
GIVEN g IS A `general arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the addition replaces other arrangements under` g IF
    NOT `the general arrangement continues` g

-- The evidence: section 3(ב) disapplies only section 3(א), the replacing
-- and cancelling; no clause of the circular withholds section 2's payment.
@desc A clause of this circular, by what it does.
DECLARE `daycare clause` IS ONE OF
    `section 2 pays the addition`
    `section 3(א) cancels other arrangements`

`the clauses section 3(ב) disapplies` MEANS LIST `section 3(א) cancels other arrangements`

`section 3(ב) does not say the addition stops` MEANS
    NOT (elem `section 2 pays the addition` `the clauses section 3(ב) disapplies`)
#ASSERT `section 3(ב) does not say the addition stops`

§§ `4 ביצוע תשלומים`

@ref akn:art_4/p1
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee`, g IS A `general arrangement`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `daycare action`
DECIDE `paying the addition with September's salary` d g IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the daycare addition` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `the daycare addition` d g
    WITHIN `month number` September
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 4: the payments are made with the September 2011 salary"

@export default The monthly daycare addition from 1.9.2011 a teaching employee of an owner is paid under circular תשע"ב/5
GIVEN d IS A `daycare employee` @desc the employee in the month
      g IS A `general arrangement` @desc any general daycare arrangement of the grade, employer, workplace or region (section 3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the daycare addition` d g IS
    IF `a parent the addition is paid to` d AND `a month the addition is paid for` d AND `the addition replaces other arrangements under` g
    THEN `the full-position daycare amount for` (d's `children under 5`) TIMES `the daycare position share` d
    ELSE 0

-- akn:art_4/p2 The contact line for questions; no rule.
-- akn:art_4/p3 The contact line, continued; no rule.
-- akn:art_4/p4 The telephone numbers; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

`a teacher at 120% with one child` MEANS
    `daycare employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of secondary education` IS TRUE
        `a mother`                           IS TRUE
        `a widower or divorced man with the children in his custody` IS FALSE
        `entitled through section 4(א) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law` IS FALSE
        `children under 5`                   IS 1
        `position fraction`                  IS 1.2
        `entitled to salary from the employer and funded by it this month` IS TRUE

`no general arrangement` MEANS `general arrangement` FALSE 0 0 TRUE
`a better general arrangement` MEANS `general arrangement` TRUE 350 600 TRUE
`a lesser general arrangement` MEANS `general arrangement` TRUE 350 450 TRUE
`a half-position mother of two` MEANS
    `daycare employee` WITH
        `in the teaching-staff grade`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of secondary education` IS TRUE
        `a mother`                           IS TRUE
        `a widower or divorced man with the children in his custody` IS FALSE
        `entitled through section 4(א) of the Equal Employment Opportunities Law` IS FALSE
        `children under 5`                   IS 2
        `position fraction`                  IS 0.5
        `entitled to salary from the employer and funded by it this month` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the daycare addition` `a half-position mother of two` `no general arrangement` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `the daycare addition` `a teacher at 120% with one child` `no general arrangement` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the daycare addition` `a half-position mother of two` `a better general arrangement` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the daycare addition` `a half-position mother of two` `a lesser general arrangement` EQUALS 250

#TRACE `paying the addition with September's salary` `a half-position mother of two` `no general arrangement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the daycare addition` 250 AT 1
#TRACE `paying the addition with September's salary` `a half-position mother of two` `no general arrangement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay the daycare addition` 250 AT 2
#TRACE `no receipts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `require receipts` AT 1
